<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  EN16931 UBL, intra-community supply issued by a Swedish supplier to a Spanish
  recipient. Two things about this document are deliberate and load-bearing.

  It prints NO Spanish anywhere: the item description and the statutory mention
  are in German, the language the issuer bills in. A reader that recovers the
  base, the cuota, both parties and the legend from this document recovers them
  from structure rather than from recognising Spanish wording.

  It is denominated in SEK, not EUR. Every figure on it is a foreign-currency
  figure, so a record minted from it that reported a euro total would be
  asserting a conversion the document never states.

  UNTDID 5305 category K with VATEX-EU-IC is the intra-community exemption
  (LIVA art. 25): a taxable base with no cuota, self-assessed by the recipient.
-->
